1
00:00:01,380 --> 00:00:02,320
Hey, guys!

2
00:00:02,620 --> 00:00:04,032
I think I see an island!

3
00:00:05,580 --> 00:00:06,410
Hmm...

4
00:00:06,493 --> 00:00:08,200
Looks uninhabited to me.

5
00:00:08,560 --> 00:00:09,680
Ready the anchor!

6
00:00:10,060 --> 00:00:11,354
Let's go check it out!

7
00:00:11,740 --> 00:00:14,337
Find me some ingredients and
I'll start cooking lunch.

8
00:00:14,420 --> 00:00:15,250
All right!

9
00:00:15,600 --> 00:00:17,894
Listen, nothing's slimy or gross, okay?

10
00:00:18,140 --> 00:00:19,097
What does it matter?

11
00:00:19,180 --> 00:00:21,157
Once it's in your stomach,
it's all the same.

12
00:00:21,240 --> 00:00:22,980
Get over yourself. Ow!

13
00:00:30,400 --> 00:00:33,117
Hey, Chopper, did you
find any new herbs to use?

14
00:00:33,200 --> 00:00:34,030
Mm-hmm.

15
00:00:34,113 --> 00:00:35,377
This place has all sorts of neat stuff.

16
00:00:35,460 --> 00:00:38,697
I got a good stock, but I'm still
looking in case I missed something.

17
00:00:38,780 --> 00:00:42,057
Which reminds me, I noticed
something weird a second ago.

18
00:00:42,140 --> 00:00:44,217
There's a little groove
along the trail here.

19
00:00:44,300 --> 00:00:45,476
I wonder what it is.

20
00:00:45,780 --> 00:00:46,677
Oh, you're right.

21
00:00:46,760 --> 00:00:47,590
That is weird.

22
00:00:47,760 --> 00:00:50,657
Looks like a bicycle or
something came through here.

23
00:00:50,740 --> 00:00:52,797
Come on, that doesn't make any sense.

24
00:00:52,880 --> 00:00:54,217
There's nobody else on the island.

25
00:00:54,300 --> 00:00:56,006
Why would there be a bicycle?

26
00:00:56,200 --> 00:00:57,729
Yeah, that's a good point.

27
00:00:58,680 --> 00:00:59,880
Hey, check it out!

28
00:01:00,040 --> 00:01:01,922
We're almost through the jungle!

29
00:01:04,040 --> 00:01:05,393
Well, that's a letdown.

30
00:01:05,560 --> 00:01:08,384
Just looks like a whole
lot of nothing out here.

31
00:01:09,980 --> 00:01:10,940
He's excited.

32
00:01:11,080 --> 00:01:12,097
Did I miss something?

33
00:01:12,180 --> 00:01:13,474
I don't get it either.

34
00:01:13,600 --> 00:01:15,400
Maybe he found some new herbs.

35
00:01:16,320 --> 00:01:17,150
Huh?

36
00:01:18,500 --> 00:01:19,597
Chopper, you cheater!

37
00:01:19,680 --> 00:01:22,397
You were gonna hog that big mushroom
all to yourself, weren't you?

38
00:01:22,480 --> 00:01:23,380
Get back here!

39
00:01:25,520 --> 00:01:27,580
Hey, what happened? Are you OK?

40
00:01:28,000 --> 00:01:29,597
There must be something behind that rock.

41
00:01:29,680 --> 00:01:30,562
Come on, hurry.

42
00:01:32,940 --> 00:01:34,760
Whoa, you're not a mushroom.

43
00:01:40,100 --> 00:01:40,930
Hmm?

44
00:01:41,400 --> 00:01:42,760
A raccoon dog.

45
00:01:43,100 --> 00:01:44,257
Can't you see the antlers?

46
00:01:44,340 --> 00:01:45,222
I'm a reindeer.

47
00:01:45,660 --> 00:01:47,580
I saw you fall. Are you hurt?

48
00:01:48,320 --> 00:01:49,720
Who the heck is that?

49
00:01:51,360 --> 00:01:52,217
What's going on?

50
00:01:52,300 --> 00:01:54,240
I don't know. Someone's here.

51
00:01:54,500 --> 00:01:55,480
Do you mind?

52
00:01:55,720 --> 00:01:56,640
I was sleeping.

53
00:01:56,900 --> 00:01:58,194
Did you hit my friend?

54
00:01:58,940 --> 00:01:59,800
Oh, man.

55
00:02:00,000 --> 00:02:01,000
That guy is huge.

56
00:02:01,220 --> 00:02:03,514
I thought we were alone on this island.

57
00:02:11,000 --> 00:02:12,040
You know him?

58
00:02:13,920 --> 00:02:15,540
Hey, is this guy an enemy?

59
00:02:15,760 --> 00:02:16,660
Who is he?

60
00:02:17,680 --> 00:02:21,260
If Robin's freaking out, then
so am I. Something's wrong.

61
00:02:22,300 --> 00:02:23,817
Whoa, whoa, whoa, hold on.

62
00:02:23,900 --> 00:02:27,157
Look, I know you're surprised to
see me, but don't get so worked up.

63
00:02:27,240 --> 00:02:29,777
It's not like I came here on
official orders or anything.

64
00:02:29,860 --> 00:02:33,760
It's a nice day, so I decided
to go for a ride. Orders, huh?

65
00:02:34,020 --> 00:02:35,608
And who is it you work for?

66
00:02:40,600 --> 00:02:41,500
My, my.

67
00:02:41,900 --> 00:02:45,018
You've grown into quite the
lovely lady, haven't you?

68
00:02:45,580 --> 00:02:46,460
Nico Robin.

69
00:03:51,820 --> 00:03:57,360
If you want to die, I will
protect you from the moment

70
00:03:58,320 --> 00:04:00,420
Okay, let's go ahead and go ahead

71
00:04:01,320 --> 00:04:03,800
The moon will always come to the moon

72
00:04:04,420 --> 00:04:11,000
The wind will come to the sky
and see the light of the sky

73
00:04:11,740 --> 00:04:12,957
Oh, oh, oh, oh,

74
00:04:13,040 --> 00:04:20,040
oh.

75
00:04:51,140 --> 00:04:55,580
This guy has Robin scared out
of her freaking mind. Why?

76
00:05:03,700 --> 00:05:05,160
He's a Marine.

77
00:05:05,900 --> 00:05:08,840
Navy Headquarters Admiral Aokiji.

78
00:05:09,440 --> 00:05:10,270
Admiral?

79
00:05:11,080 --> 00:05:13,256
Wait, you mean this guy's an admiral?

80
00:05:13,440 --> 00:05:15,852
That's one of the highest ranks there is.

81
00:05:17,260 --> 00:05:18,090
That's right.

82
00:05:18,180 --> 00:05:19,997
There are only three
officers in the entire

83
00:05:20,080 --> 00:05:22,904
Navy who currently hold
the position of admiral.

84
00:05:25,380 --> 00:05:28,040
Akainu, Aokiji, and Kizaru.

85
00:05:29,460 --> 00:05:34,017
The only one who outbreaks them is Fleet
Admiral Sengoku, the Navy's top official.

86
00:05:34,100 --> 00:05:36,597
The man you see standing
before you is one of the three

87
00:05:36,680 --> 00:05:40,033
men known as the world
government's ultimate powerhouses.

88
00:05:40,500 --> 00:05:43,337
But why in the heck is
someone like this even here?

89
00:05:43,420 --> 00:05:45,477
Should you be out hunting
some big-time pirates

90
00:05:45,560 --> 00:05:48,177
with a bazillion berry
bounties or something?

91
00:05:48,260 --> 00:05:49,090
Go away.

92
00:05:49,740 --> 00:05:50,570
Huh?

93
00:05:51,940 --> 00:05:53,060
Oh, my, my.

94
00:05:53,460 --> 00:05:57,780
Another very sexy lady with super
big bazongas. Are you free tonight?

95
00:05:58,100 --> 00:06:02,000
You watch your mouth, you lanky
jerk! Hey, focus! Pay attention!

96
00:06:02,680 --> 00:06:05,160
Whoa, whoa, hold on a second, you guys.

97
00:06:05,360 --> 00:06:07,037
Didn't you hear what I just said?

98
00:06:07,120 --> 00:06:09,238
I'm just out taking a little stroll.

99
00:06:09,880 --> 00:06:11,720
Don't get so worked up, okay?

100
00:06:12,020 --> 00:06:18,240
I mean, you guys are just, you're like
just whatchamacallits, you know? What?

101
00:06:20,860 --> 00:06:22,420
I forgot. Oh, well.

102
00:06:22,700 --> 00:06:25,053
You're not making any sense, you weirdo!

103
00:06:25,160 --> 00:06:26,317
Robin, are you kidding?

104
00:06:26,400 --> 00:06:28,257
You must be mistaken him for someone else.

105
00:06:28,340 --> 00:06:31,637
This doofus wouldn't pass for a
regular Marine, let alone an Admiral.

106
00:06:31,720 --> 00:06:32,560
Hey, come on.

107
00:06:32,680 --> 00:06:36,504
You shouldn't go around judging
people based on their appearance.

108
00:06:37,040 --> 00:06:41,900
The motto I've always lived by as a
Marine is total, slovenly justice.

109
00:06:42,180 --> 00:06:43,827
Then our judgment was right!

110
00:06:44,020 --> 00:06:45,680
Anyway, what I was saying...

111
00:06:46,580 --> 00:06:47,960
Excuse me a moment.

112
00:06:49,100 --> 00:06:52,140
Being on my feet too long
makes me tired. Yeah?

113
00:06:52,380 --> 00:06:55,257
Then maybe you shouldn't have been
sleeping standing up, you think?

114
00:06:55,340 --> 00:06:57,857
What I was saying is
that I have no intention

115
00:06:57,940 --> 00:07:00,097
of capturing you or anything like that,

116
00:07:00,180 --> 00:07:01,415
so just take it easy.

117
00:07:01,660 --> 00:07:04,877
I'm only here to confirm the
whereabouts of Nico Robin,

118
00:07:04,960 --> 00:07:07,837
who hadn't been seen since
the Alabasta incident.

119
00:07:07,920 --> 00:07:10,096
As we suspected, she's been with you.

120
00:07:10,320 --> 00:07:12,400
That is one tall piece of apathy.

121
00:07:12,640 --> 00:07:15,337
The only thing high-ranking
about him is his nerve.

122
00:07:15,420 --> 00:07:18,837
I'll put some sort of report
together for headquarters later.

123
00:07:18,920 --> 00:07:22,817
Now that you've added another crew
member who's got a price on her head,

124
00:07:22,900 --> 00:07:24,800
your overall bounty has gone up.

125
00:07:25,100 --> 00:07:31,160
$100 million plus $60 million
plus $79 million equals...

126
00:07:33,400 --> 00:07:34,580
Ah, screw it.

127
00:07:34,680 --> 00:07:35,880
Some big-ass number.

128
00:07:36,000 --> 00:07:37,294
Just do the damn math.

129
00:07:38,700 --> 00:07:42,140
That's it! Come, come!
Hold on, Yippie! Stop it!

130
00:07:44,360 --> 00:07:46,500
What are you guys doing? Let me go!

131
00:07:46,760 --> 00:07:48,717
Why are you trying to start
a fight with this guy?

132
00:07:48,800 --> 00:07:49,630
Are you crazy?

133
00:07:49,713 --> 00:07:51,297
He's one of the strongest
Marines there is!

134
00:07:51,380 --> 00:07:55,177
I'm not just gonna stand around while this
jerk tries to take Robin away from us!

135
00:07:55,260 --> 00:07:56,280
Take it easy.

136
00:07:56,460 --> 00:07:58,797
I told you I'm not gonna
do anything, remember?

137
00:07:58,880 --> 00:08:04,337
I told you I'm just

138
00:08:04,420 --> 00:08:06,317
out on a stroll stroll

139
00:08:06,400 --> 00:08:08,637
huh go take your stroll somewhere else

140
00:08:08,720 --> 00:08:13,760
get out of here why are you so angry at
me looks like he's trying to pick a fight

141
00:08:18,960 --> 00:08:21,537
so you're really a
marine I wish we'd known

142
00:08:21,620 --> 00:08:24,640
that a lot sooner hey
who are all these people

143
00:08:25,580 --> 00:08:27,080
Whoa, are you guys okay?

144
00:08:27,380 --> 00:08:29,615
I thought this island was uninhabited.

145
00:08:30,060 --> 00:08:34,237
Well, they're probably castaways
that washed up on the shore here.

146
00:08:34,320 --> 00:08:37,937
There was a passenger liner that was
reported missing about a month ago.

147
00:08:38,020 --> 00:08:39,937
Last seen somewhere in this area.

148
00:08:40,020 --> 00:08:41,477
I'm guessing it sank.

149
00:08:41,560 --> 00:08:43,207
And these are the survivors.

150
00:08:48,140 --> 00:08:49,457
Okay, whatever.

151
00:08:49,540 --> 00:08:52,117
I'll leave, but before I do.

152
00:08:52,200 --> 00:08:55,847
You guys should gather your stuff
and get ready to leave, too.

153
00:08:56,940 --> 00:09:01,217
Fortunately, I know of an inhabited island
that's not too far away from this one.

154
00:09:01,300 --> 00:09:04,182
You should go there and
ask them to help you out.

155
00:09:05,140 --> 00:09:06,300
Hey, you guys!

156
00:09:06,520 --> 00:09:07,937
Don't believe a word he says!

157
00:09:08,020 --> 00:09:08,850
Understand me?

158
00:09:08,940 --> 00:09:10,646
This jerk's a marine officer!

159
00:09:13,800 --> 00:09:15,540
So what? Is that a problem?

160
00:09:19,400 --> 00:09:21,080
Oh, that's right. I get it.

161
00:09:21,260 --> 00:09:22,357
I guess that makes sense.

162
00:09:22,440 --> 00:09:26,917
Normally, the Marines are your friends
and the Pirates are the bad guys, right?

163
00:09:27,000 --> 00:09:29,020
Stop it! What's so funny? Him?

164
00:09:29,180 --> 00:09:31,940
How is he going to help
anybody? I don't know.

165
00:09:32,100 --> 00:09:34,017
Heck, I don't even think he has a ship.

166
00:09:34,100 --> 00:09:37,097
Other than ours, there isn't
another ship around anywhere.

167
00:09:37,180 --> 00:09:38,010
Let's see.

168
00:09:38,093 --> 00:09:40,937
There's no ship and nobody here
seems to have a Log Pose either.

169
00:09:41,020 --> 00:09:43,637
How in the world are they supposed
to get to that island anyway?

170
00:09:43,720 --> 00:09:45,040
Oh, they'll be fine.

171
00:09:45,540 --> 00:09:48,364
Nothing you say sounds
the least bit convincing.

172
00:09:48,720 --> 00:09:49,550
It's true.

173
00:09:51,960 --> 00:09:54,078
He does have the power to help them.

174
00:10:05,840 --> 00:10:06,960
That should do it!

175
00:10:07,240 --> 00:10:09,117
We loaded them up with food and water.

176
00:10:09,200 --> 00:10:11,457
It should be enough to last
them for quite a while.

177
00:10:11,540 --> 00:10:14,017
Feels good to do a little
work from time to time.

178
00:10:14,100 --> 00:10:15,457
Yeah, no doubt about that!

179
00:10:15,540 --> 00:10:16,370
Hey, you know something?

180
00:10:16,453 --> 00:10:17,339
You're not so bad.

181
00:10:17,920 --> 00:10:18,817
What do you know?

182
00:10:18,900 --> 00:10:20,157
They're hitting it off.

183
00:10:20,240 --> 00:10:21,360
Okay, so now what?

184
00:10:21,460 --> 00:10:22,957
Are you going to swim
to that island to drag

185
00:10:23,040 --> 00:10:24,877
these guys and all their stuff behind you?

186
00:10:24,960 --> 00:10:26,140
Don't be ridiculous.

187
00:10:28,780 --> 00:10:30,760
All right, everybody, stay back.

188
00:10:54,500 --> 00:10:55,700
What is that thing?

189
00:10:55,880 --> 00:10:57,357
It's some kind of monster!

190
00:10:57,440 --> 00:11:00,264
I bet it's the guardian
of this part of the sea!

191
00:11:05,980 --> 00:11:06,810
Hey, you!

192
00:11:07,000 --> 00:11:08,580
Run for it! Look out!

193
00:11:08,680 --> 00:11:09,680
Get out of there!

194
00:11:14,080 --> 00:11:15,040
Ice Age.

195
00:11:28,800 --> 00:11:30,600
A Devil Fruit.

196
00:11:38,940 --> 00:11:43,220
The sea, it's frozen.

197
00:11:44,440 --> 00:11:47,840
This is the power of a
Navy Headquarters Admiral.

198
00:12:07,320 --> 00:12:09,860
It'll stay like that for at least a week.

199
00:12:14,200 --> 00:12:17,720
Head out across the sea in
that direction. Take your time.

200
00:12:18,000 --> 00:12:20,765
You should reach the
island in about four days.

201
00:12:24,300 --> 00:12:29,241
It's going to be a little on the chilly
side, so be sure to bundle up and stay warm.

202
00:12:29,740 --> 00:12:32,400
Is this a dream?

203
00:12:34,020 --> 00:12:36,520
The sea has become as hard as the ground.

204
00:12:37,500 --> 00:12:39,300
We can finally cross it.

205
00:12:39,600 --> 00:12:41,557
Now we'll be able to
get off of this island.

206
00:12:41,640 --> 00:12:42,740
Thank you!

207
00:12:42,940 --> 00:12:44,080
Thanks so much!

208
00:12:44,400 --> 00:12:46,640
It's a miracle!

209
00:12:47,120 --> 00:12:49,002
The Marine granted us a miracle!

210
00:13:01,040 --> 00:13:02,500
All right, then.

211
00:13:02,820 --> 00:13:04,291
Time for us to get going.

212
00:13:04,380 --> 00:13:05,210
Right.

213
00:13:05,293 --> 00:13:07,460
I'm really happy for you guys. Take care.

214
00:13:07,780 --> 00:13:10,397
I guess there are all sorts
of different pirates, huh?

215
00:13:10,480 --> 00:13:13,697
How can we ever thank you for
everything that you've done for us?

216
00:13:13,780 --> 00:13:15,937
Not only did you treat
our sick and injured,

217
00:13:16,020 --> 00:13:18,617
but you shared your food
and water with us as well.

218
00:13:18,700 --> 00:13:20,171
Aw, don't worry about it.

219
00:13:20,800 --> 00:13:22,657
Good things happen to good people.

220
00:13:22,740 --> 00:13:24,237
Just let fate take its course.

221
00:13:24,320 --> 00:13:26,257
Make sure the children don't catch cold.

222
00:13:26,340 --> 00:13:27,677
Keep them bundled up tight.

223
00:13:27,760 --> 00:13:31,457
At any rate, these colder temperatures
should keep your food fresh longer.

224
00:13:31,540 --> 00:13:33,020
Thank you all very much.

225
00:13:33,180 --> 00:13:35,239
We will never forget your kindness.

226
00:13:35,660 --> 00:13:38,200
Take care, Straw Hat pirates! Bye!

227
00:13:38,820 --> 00:13:40,000
Take care, boys!

228
00:13:41,280 --> 00:13:42,960
Be careful on your trip!

229
00:13:43,180 --> 00:13:44,780
Safe journeys to pies!

230
00:13:45,960 --> 00:13:47,700
That felt really good.

231
00:13:48,880 --> 00:13:51,560
It feels like winter just happened.

232
00:13:52,120 --> 00:13:54,000
Check it out! I can skate!

233
00:13:54,380 --> 00:13:55,560
Awesome, jumper!

234
00:13:56,900 --> 00:13:59,100
Man, it's cold. I'm freezing.

235
00:14:05,700 --> 00:14:06,800
What is it?

236
00:14:07,040 --> 00:14:08,437
How should I put this?

237
00:14:08,520 --> 00:14:11,820
You're the spitting image of
your grandfather, Monkey D.

238
00:14:11,920 --> 00:14:12,750
Luffy.

239
00:14:13,280 --> 00:14:18,100
Or maybe I should say you're just
as reckless and hard to figure out.

240
00:14:18,820 --> 00:14:20,940
You knew my grandpa?

241
00:14:22,500 --> 00:14:23,780
Seriously? Luffy's?

242
00:14:27,400 --> 00:14:28,940
Hey, Luffy, what's wrong?

243
00:14:29,120 --> 00:14:30,061
You're sweating.

244
00:14:30,380 --> 00:14:31,400
Uh, nothing.

245
00:14:31,640 --> 00:14:33,100
Really, I'm fine.

246
00:14:33,280 --> 00:14:36,680
Your grandfather helped me
out once, a long time ago.

247
00:14:37,000 --> 00:14:38,260
That's why I'm here.

248
00:14:38,520 --> 00:14:43,000
I wanted to see you and Nico
Robin together with my own eyes.

249
00:14:44,460 --> 00:14:48,420
On second thought, maybe
I should just kill you.

250
00:14:49,240 --> 00:14:52,320
The government still doesn't
consider you a threat,

251
00:14:52,560 --> 00:14:56,520
but I know enough of your history
to see you're a formidable crew.

252
00:14:57,100 --> 00:15:01,740
You may be few in number, but with
the shrewd rogues gathered here,

253
00:15:01,960 --> 00:15:05,080
this crew will likely
be a problem later on.

254
00:15:05,780 --> 00:15:09,217
Considering the circumstances
regarding your initial bounty,

255
00:15:09,300 --> 00:15:14,065
the numerous daring actions you've taken,
and the speed of your overall progress.

256
00:15:14,360 --> 00:15:16,697
I've fought outlaws for most of my life,

257
00:15:16,780 --> 00:15:20,337
but thinking about how you'll turn
out scares the hell out of me.

258
00:15:20,420 --> 00:15:22,067
Hey, wait, hold on a second!

259
00:15:22,360 --> 00:15:25,357
